# Settings for the Winlink packet modem (Dire Wolf), copy to direwolf.env; see docs/winlink.md. It is a separate file from
# winlink.env on purpose: Dire Wolf decodes whatever it hears on the air, so it is given only what it uses and none of the gateway's
# passwords. Never put MOR_WINLINK_ADMIN_PASSWORD or MOR_WINLINK_CMS_PASSWORD here.
#
# If you already have a winlink.env, `sh ./split-winlink-env.sh` (setup.sh and update.sh run it) makes this file from it.
#
# Your callsign and the SSID the modem is named with (the gateway answers as CALL-SSID, usually -10). A GMRS callsign is refused.
# Keep these the same as in winlink.env.
# MOR_WINLINK_CALL=W1AW
# MOR_WINLINK_SSID=10
#
# The packet radio's PTT: none (a radio with VOX) or cm108 (a CM108-type or AIOC interface; set MOR_PACKET_PTT_HIDRAW in .env to its
# name, /dev/moreopenrepeater-packet from ./setup.sh --packet-radio, and the GPIO pin it keys with).
# MOR_PACKET_PTT=none
# MOR_PACKET_PTT_GPIO=3
# The packet radio's sound card number, MOR_PACKET_CARD, and its PTT device, MOR_PACKET_PTT_HIDRAW, are set in .env (they are
# the host's devices, not settings of the modem).
